  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Conflict Affected Communities in Cameroon&#x2019;s Far-North and North-West, South-West Regions to Recover through Resilience Building and Reconciliation for the Humanitarian Development Peace Nexus</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian needs in Cameroon remain high. According to the Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) published in April 2022, approximately 3.9 million people (or one in six) are in need of emergency assistance as the country has three humanitarian fronts (Far North Region, North-West, South-West (NWSW) Regions and East refugee crisis) to cope with, in addition to the war in Ukraine which has suddenly increased instability with higher food prices that have compounded community pressures and pushed vulnerable persons further into poverty and hunger.  This project provides a third phase in Cameroon for IOM to build community resilience and recovery to save lives in Cameroon&apos;s crisis areas of Far North and NWSW. The objective of this project is to ensure that displaced populations and vulnerable youth and host community members in Cameroon have access to the urgent assistance that they need to ensure their pathways to greater recovery and community resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
